  "question": {
    "text": "If <math><mi>p</mi></math> represents radiation pressure, <math><mi>C</mi></math> represents the speed of light and <math><mi>q</mi></math> represents radiation energy striking a unit area per second, then non-zero integers <math><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></math> and <math><mi>c</mi></math> are such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><msup><mi>C</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></math> is dimensionless, then"
  },
